If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder-sign then every clinician should address a patient-concern with the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder then every clinician should ensure an evidence-based-medication-treatment for the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder-sign then every clinician should use a nonpharmacologic-pain-treatment for the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder-sign then every clinician should use a pharmacologic-pain-treatment for the patient.
